{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass_formula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass_formula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.not_pair_skein_mass_formula_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.not_pair_skein_mass_formula_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass/pair_skein_mass_formula.lean#L146-L155","doc":"**The formula is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it is\nnamed rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nAt `q = 1` with all dressed masses zero the right-hand side is `0`, so a pair\nSkein mass of `1` fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_difference","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass/pair_skein_mass_formula.lean#L128-L144","doc":"**Species exchange is antisymmetric with the Skein coefficient** —\nderived, not assumed.\n\n    𝒮_ab − 𝒮_ba = (q − q⁻¹)(μ_a − μ_b) / (q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}).\n\nThe factor `q − q⁻¹` is the Skein-relation coefficient\n(`σ − σ⁻¹ = q − q⁻¹`, AGENTS.md §7a), which is precisely what the\nmanuscript's description of the crossing weights asserts. Obtaining it as a\ntheorem is the reason the formula is worth naming. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.pair_skein_mass_formula","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass/pair_skein_mass_formula.lean#L115-L126","doc":"**The pair Skein mass formula** ([`lem:pair-skein-mass-formula`]), as a\nproposition over caller-supplied data:\n\n    𝒮_{ab}(q) = (q μ_a + q⁻¹ μ_b) / (q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}).\n\n**Named, not asserted.**  See the module docstring for the convention-C\nscoping and for what the identity would need in order to be about the\ncategorical pair Skein mass rather than about reals. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:pair-skein-mass-formula","label":"lem:pair-skein-mass-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/pair-skein-mass-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.two_le_normaliser","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.two_le_normaliser","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass/pair_skein_mass_formula.lean#L99-L113","doc":"**The normaliser never vanishes**: for `q > 0` it is at least `2`, with\nequality exactly at `q = 1` (AM–GM on `√q`).\n\nDerived, and load-bearing: Lean's `x / 0 = 0` would otherwise let the pair\nSkein mass formula hold vacuously wherever the normaliser vanished. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.skeinNormaliserC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.skeinNormaliserC","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass/pair_skein_mass_formula.lean#L91-L97","doc":"The Markov normaliser `q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}` of the pair Skein mass.\n\n**Convention C.**  Its reciprocal is `√q/(q+1) = z_C`, not the canonical\n`z_D = q³/(q²+1)` — see the module docstring.  Named so the convention is\nvisible at the use site rather than buried in a division. ","signatureChunk":0}]}